  "notes": [
    "Transcribed by hand from the pages above on the retrieval date. Always confirm against the live AMD documentation before relying on a result.",
    "Every rule carries a 'ref' list naming entries in 'references': the exact page, section and row, the ROCm version that page describes, the transcription date and the date the rule was last re-checked against that page. A reference that could not be re-checked has verification 'unverified' and says why.",
    "The system-requirements page still describes ROCm 7.14, while this snapshot describes 10.2.0. Facts only that page lists (OS entries with source 'sysreq', kernels_sysreq_only, gpus_sysreq_only: e.g. RHEL 10.1/9.7, Ubuntu 24.04 kernel 6.17, MI210 on Debian 12) count as PASS only on a host running ROCm 7.14; on any other host, or when ROCm is not detected, they give WARNING. Point-release labels that differ between the pages (Ubuntu 24.04.4 vs 24.04.5) are both recorded; OS releases are matched by major.minor.",
    "os_gpu_restrictions name individual products, because GPUs that share an LLVM target can differ (e.g. MI300X and MI300A on Debian 13). Where the 10.2.0 matrix and the 7.14 system requirements disagree about a GPU on an OS, the matrix decides; a GPU only the 7.14 page lists is in gpus_sysreq_only and follows the rule above.",
    "Ryzen APU targets are listed under targets_uncertain and produce WARNING, never PASS: the 10.2.0 matrix names each APU's LLVM target, but a detected iGPU name can map to more than one target (Radeon 840M is gfx1152 or gfx1153), and KernelVet does not model the APU operating-system and driver rows.",
    "ROCm 10.x versions HIP separately from ROCm (ROCm 10.2.0 ships HIP 7.17.0). hip_versions records the HIP version each ROCm 10.x release lists in its 'ROCm Core SDK components' table.",
    "Changes from the 10.1.0 snapshot (2026-11-18): the 10.2.0 matrix adds Instinct MI350P, Radeon PRO W7900D, RHEL 10.3, RHEL 9.9, SLES 16.1, amdgpu 31.70.0, PyTorch 2.15 and JAX 0.11.2; it drops amdgpu 30.20.1, 30.20.0 and 30.10.2 (Instinct) and 31.50.0 (Radeon), and lists only RHEL 10.3 and 9.9 for Radeon. MI350P, RX 9050, RX 9050 (4GB), RX 7600, Radeon AI PRO R9700S and R9600 were already in the 10.1.0 selector but missing from that snapshot; they are now included.",
    "Per AMD: if a GPU is not listed it is not officially supported."
  ],
